          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A connected limit is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            that has just one
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            of two objects is not a connected limit because the relevant diagram has two connected components. A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong connected limit
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            over a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected category
            %strong connected colimit
            is a colimit over a connected category.
